# Build context for Dockerfile.aio is the repo root, which has no
# .dockerignore of its own. Without this the daemon would receive the whole
# tree — around 500 MB, most of it backend/.venv.
#
# BuildKit prefers <dockerfile>.dockerignore over the context root's, so this
# is scoped to the all-in-one build and changes nothing for the existing
# backend/ and frontend/ builds.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
.git
.github
frontend/dist
backend/data
# backend/.dockerignore omits these, so a locally built backend image bakes in
# whatever beat state the developer happened to have.
backend/celerybeat-schedule*
secrets
docs
charts
tmp
**/.env
